# Module: MaintActivityCodes

## MaintActivityCodes-UC1 — View Activity Codes

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: User navigates to the Activity Codes maintenance page.
- Description: The user views the list of activity codes.
- Preconditions: User is logged in with appropriate access rights.
- Postconditions: The activity codes are displayed in a grid view.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User navigates to the Activity Codes page.
  2. The system displays the list of activity codes.
  3. User can scroll through the list as necessary.
- Extensions: None
- Exceptions:
  - If no data is found, a "No Data" message is displayed.
- Business Rules:
  - Only users with specific access rights can view activity codes.
- Assumptions: User has permission to view the maintenance page.
- Open Issues: None

## MaintActivityCodes-UC2 — Add New Activity Code

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: User clicks the "Add" button.
- Description: The user adds a new activity code to the system.
- Preconditions: User has edit permissions.
- Postconditions: The new activity code is stored in the system.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User clicks on "Add" button.
  2. System displays detail entry form.
  3. User enters the name and short name for the new activity code.
  4. User clicks "Save".
  5. System validates data and saves the new activity code.
  6. System updates the view to display the new entry.
- Extensions:
  - [3a] If user cancels, changes are not saved.
- Exceptions:
  - [5a] If validation fails, display error message and prompt for corrections.
- Business Rules:
  - Both name and short name are required fields.
- Assumptions: User understands the data requirements for activity codes.
- Open Issues: None

## MaintActivityCodes-UC3 — Edit Existing Activity Code

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: User selects an activity code and clicks "Edit".
- Description: The user modifies an existing activity code.
- Preconditions: User has edit permissions.
- Postconditions: The activity code is updated in the system.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User selects an activity code from the list.
  2. User clicks "Edit".
  3. System displays the selected activity code’s details for editing.
  4. User modifies the details.
  5. User clicks "Save".
  6. System validates changes and updates the activity code.
  7. System reflects updated information in the view.
- Extensions:
  - [4a] If user cancels, changes are not saved.
- Exceptions:
  - [6a] If validation fails, display error message and prompt for corrections.
- Business Rules:
  - Both name and short name are required fields for edit.
- Assumptions: User is aware of editing capabilities and constraints.
- Open Issues: None

## MaintActivityCodes-UC4 — Delete Activity Code

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: User selects an activity code and clicks "Delete".
- Description: The user deletes an activity code.
- Preconditions: User has appropriate permissions to delete.
- Postconditions: Selected activity code is marked as inactive.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User selects an activity code from the list.
  2. User clicks "Delete".
  3. System prompts for confirmation.
  4. User confirms deletion.
  5. System marks the activity code as inactive (soft delete).
  6. System updates the view to reflect the change.
- Extensions:
  - None
- Exceptions:
  - [3a] If user cancels at the confirmation prompt, deletion does not occur.
- Business Rules:
  - Only inactive status is applied, code remains in the database.
- Assumptions: System uses a soft delete mechanism.
- Open Issues: None

## MaintActivityCodes-UC5 — Reactivate Activity Code

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: User selects an inactive activity code and clicks "Reactivate".
- Description: The user reactivates an inactive activity code.
- Preconditions: User has appropriate permissions to reactivate.
- Postconditions: Activity code status is changed to active.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User selects an inactive activity code from the list.
  2. User clicks "Reactivate".
  3. System confirms reactivation.
  4. System changes the status of the activity code to active.
  5. System updates the view to demonstrate the change.
- Extensions: None
- Exceptions: None
- Business Rules:
  - Only users with administrative rights can reactivate.
- Assumptions: System supports status changes for activity codes.
- Open Issues: None

## MaintActivityCodes-UC6 — Refresh View of Activity Codes

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: User clicks the "Refresh" button.
- Description: The user refreshes the view to see the most up-to-date list of activity codes.
- Preconditions: User is on the Activity Codes maintenance page.
- Postconditions: The list view is updated with the latest data.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User clicks "Refresh".
  2. System pulls the latest data from the database.
  3. System updates the view with current information.
- Extensions: None
- Exceptions: None
- Business Rules: None
- Assumptions: Data has potentially changed since the page was loaded.
- Open Issues: None